 was verified.","status":"argued"},{"changed_at":"2026-08-29T20:06:17.004695Z","explanation":"An official oral-argument transcript was verified.","status":"argued"},{"changed_at":"2026-08-29T23:57:19.752194Z","explanation":"An official Court opinion was verified.","status":"decided"}],"case_status":"decided","dek":"The dispute centers on whether a debtor must personally intend fraud to lose discharge protection.","dek_sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 11-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 11-7"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 64, lines 19-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 64, lines 19-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 80, lines 23-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 80, lines 23-7"}],"dispositions":[],"latest_court_document_date":"2022-12-06T00:00:00Z","maturity":"post_opinion","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2022","official_disposition_urls":["https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/22pdf/598us1r5_1b72.pdf"],"official_docket_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/docket/docketfiles/html/public/21-908.html","primary_docket":"21-908","revisions":[{"correction_note":"Rewritten to the concise citizen-facing editorial standard.","created_at":"2026-08-30T16:33:33.656164Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":1},{"correction_note":"Migrated to the dated official Court activity contract without model use.","created_at":"2026-09-05T03:22:24Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":2}],"schema_version":"1.1","sections":[{"heading":"What this case is about","paragraphs":["This case tests the scope of the bankruptcy fraud exception. It asks if a debtor's personal intent matters when state law already found fraud."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 11-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 11-7"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 64, lines 19-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 64, lines 19-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 80, lines 23-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 80, lines 23-7"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on December 6, 2022."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 11-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 11-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 84, lines 9-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 84, lines 9-11"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["the side that brought the case wants the debt discharged because she lacked personal intent to defraud.","the opposing side wants the debt discharged denied because the debt stems from actual fraud."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 11-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 11-7"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 64, lines 19-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 64, lines 19-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 80, lines 23-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 80, lines 23-7"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["the side that brought the case argues the statute requires the debtor to personally commit the fraud.","the opposing side argues the statute bars discharge for any debt obtained by actual fraud."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 11-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 11-7"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/21-908_dc8e.pdf","page_label":